1. What is the Java Collections Framework? 
The Collections Framework is a set of classes and interfaces used to store and manipulate groups of 
objects. 
2. Why do we use collections?  
Collections make it easier to store, search, sort, and process multiple objects. 
3. What is an ArrayList?  ArrayList is a resizable array that stores elements dynamically. 
4. What is a user-defined class? 
A class created by the programmer is called a user-defined class. Here, Student is a user-defined class. 
