6. What is an Iterator? An Iterator is used to traverse elements of a collection one by one. 
7. What is a Map?  A Map stores data in key-value pairs. 
8. What is HashMap?  
HashMap is an implementation of the Map interface that stores key-value pairs. 
9. What is RandomAccess? 
RandomAccess is a marker interface indicating that a list supports efficient direct access using an index. 
10. Does ArrayList implement RandomAccess?  Yes. 
