12. What is a String in Java?  A String is an object representing a sequence of characters. 
13. Is String mutable or immutable?  String is immutable. 
14. What does getChars() do?  
It copies selected characters from a String into a character array. 
15. What does toCharArray() do?  It converts a String into a character array. 
16. What does compareTo() return when two Strings are equal? 0 
17. What is StringBuffer?  class used to create a mutable sequence of characters. 
18.What does length() return? It returns the number of characters currently present in the buffer. 
19. What does charAt() do?   It returns the character at a specified index. 
20. What does setCharAt() do?  It changes the character at a specified index. 
21. What does setLength() do?  It changes the length of the StringBuffer. 
22. What does append() do?   It adds data at the end of the buffer. 
23. What does insert() do?   It inserts data at a specified position. 
24. What does reverse() do?   It reverses the characters in the buffer. 
25. What does delete(start, end) do?  It deletes characters from start to end - 1. 
26. What does deleteCharAt() do?   It deletes one character at the specified index. 
27. What does replace() do in StringBuffer? It replaces characters in the specified range. 
28. What does toString() do?  It converts a StringBuffer into a String. 
29. What is Swing?    Swing is a Java GUI toolkit used to create desktop applications. 
30. What is JFrame?   JFrame represents the main window of a Swing application. 
31. What is JButton?   JButton is a GUI component used to create a button. 
32. What is JLabel?    JLabel is used to display text or an image. 
33. What is event handling? 
Event handling is the process of responding to actions performed by the user, such as clicking a button. 
34. What is an ActionEvent? 
An ActionEvent is generated when an action such as a button click occurs. 
35. What is ActionListener?  ActionListener is an interface used to handle action events. 
36. What is JDBC?    JDBC stands for Java Database Connectivity. 
37. Why is JDBC used?   It allows Java programs to connect to and interact with databases. 
38. What is a JDBC driver?  A JDBC driver allows Java to communicate with a particular database. 
39. What is JSP?    JavaServer Pages. It is used to create dynamic web pages using Java. 
40. What is the difference between JSP and Java? 
Java is a programming language, while JSP is a server-side web technology that allows Java-based dynamic 
web content. 
41. What is the role of Tomcat? 
Apache Tomcat is a web server and servlet container that runs JSP and Servlet applications. 
